{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112041","id":2947906388,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6vtXtU","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112041","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112041.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112041.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112041","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112041/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112041/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112041/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/5482b9e89ec8427a76a462b1fb1af13ca0046a17","number":112041,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Tests: Convert test headers to compilation files","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"- Helps address #111218\r\n- Alternative to #108415\r\n\r\nIt's no secret that `test_main.cpp` is, by a significant margin, the most header-intensive file in the repository. This is on account of it including the contents of **every single test**, as they've been setup in headers. Moving to compilation units would be preferable, but that means that the tests themselves would fail to link, as a result of those scripts being isolated. In trying to look for workarounds, I took to the doctest repo itself and found out how they managed this process in [CMake](https://github.com/doctest/doctest/blob/master/examples/exe_with_static_libs/doctest_force_link_static_lib_in_target.cmake).\r\n\r\nOne SCons-reimplementation later, and everything actually works! Now all a designated test file has to do is include the define `TEST_FORCE_LINK()` and pass the name of the file; generator scripts will take care of the rest. No need to redeclare our entire library setup or an immediate need to resolve all encapsulation issues, so the transition isn't nearly as messy as I thought it would be.\r\n\r\nThere's a lot of changes made in this PR, but that's an inevitability when retooling this many files to be compilation files instead of headers. Several headers had to be added to compilation files, as they no longer included everything transitively. Transitive includes are still somewhat of an issue thanks to `test_macros.h`, but that can be handled in a followup PR.\r\n\r\n~~Two tests had to be suppressed after the conversion: `[Variant] Utility functions` and `[ClassDB] Add exposed classes, builtin types, and global enums`. The silver lining is I'm now reasonably certain that these two are the culprits behind our tests occasionally hanging for hours, as both consistently recreate the failure states when active. Though for whatever reason, the results are often amplified, with both cases outright segfaulting. Both absolutely warrant a more thorough dive, but that is beyond the scope of this PR & most likely would go over my head.~~ **EDIT:** Tested out on a separate branch and compilation worked again, so this might've been a false positive. Will keep an eye on.\r\n\r\n**NOTE:** This conversion excludes module tests, as they'd be a more involved process than the base tests. As such, `#include \"modules/modules_tests.gen.h\"` remains unchanged, meaning `test_main.cpp` still has *some* header bloat for the time being. Now that I know this is possible, a followup PR will take care of the module tests once this is merged.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098009,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwMDk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:buildsystem","name":"topic:buildsystem","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2231593685,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMjMxNTkzNjg1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:tests","name":"topic:tests","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2304948121,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMzA0OTQ4MTIx","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:codestyle","name":"topic:codestyle","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":14236899,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A2Tzj","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/24","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/24","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/24/labels","number":24,"state":"closed","title":"4.7","description":"","creat